Learned counsel for the appellant further submitted that in the instant case the respondents adopted a very cursory and perfunctory approach while dealing with the prospects of employment of the appellant and none of the following factors were taken into consideration before rejecting the candidature :-
(i) the nature of allegations;
(ii) overt act alleged against candidate;
(iii) whether the allegations are solely against individual candidate or have been alleged with the aid of Section 34/149 of IPC;
(iv) the criminal antecedent of the candidate;
(v) overall reputation of the candidate in his locality/society etc.
